  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-handler-attributes:getting-the-current-value-of-the-event-handler says:\n\n> and on getting, must return the result of getting the current value of the event handler in question (this can throw an exception, in which case the getting propagates it to the caller, it does not catch it).\n\nI'm not sure what a \"getting\" is and how it propagates to the caller.  As far as \"getting the current value of the event handler\" throwing... it can't.  Step 2 obvious can't throw.  In step 1, there is exceptiony stuff in substep 7, but it is in fact caught/handled/whatever.  Then there is the stuff in substep 9.  The `NewObjectEnvironment` calls can't throw in the ES spec, and neither can the `FunctionAllocate` under `FunctionCreate`.  `FunctionInitialize` _could_ in theory throw if `DefinePropertyOrThrow` throws, but that can't throw because of the assert in step 1 of `FunctionInitialize`.  Note that I'm ignoring the fact that OOM error can always be thrown, but I expect in practice UAs catch/report them inside \"getting the current value of the event handler\" and return null.\n\n@domenic @annevk \n",
